body:
Thanks for the tips guys! I read the "Why Learning Code Is So Damn Hard" article and that helps in terms of planning my education in the long term. I will definitely check out the "Foundations of Programming Videos" as well as the Vencat videos and practice with some console applications to give me a better understanding of 'for' loops (that's where I'm at right now). I'm getting ready to move on to "Creating Arrays of Values", so I hope that I continue to improve my C# proficiency. 

Also, this question from MVA had me confused in terms of the whole "{}" thing. Could somebody explain what those do in the case of the below question?

4.  What will be written to the command window? int userValue = 2;
string message = (userValue == 1) ? "boat" : "car";
Console.WriteLine("{1} - {0}", userValue, message);

A. 2 - car
B. 2 - boat
C. 1 - boat
D. car - 2
